From 0bab5aa245e2e5e2ed6e5da62622f0aa19e4f924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:56:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/23] BananaDS perf: at 2x the four quarters of a 3D line
 share one painter's pass over the 2D layers (render.2d_quarters)

At render.scale=2 a line that shows the 3D layer is composited four times, once per quarter, each a full
painter's pass over every layer: the 2D thread's biggest own cost (Composite, 599k instructions a frame on
dsstress L5 under qemu, a third of the thread's own work; Golden Sun's field: CompositeTo 49% of the thread). The
four passes differ only in the 3D layer's line. Now the layers below the 3D one are painted onto the base once
(BelowTop and BelowSec, the pixel under it), the layers above it onto nothing once (AboveTop, AboveSec: nonzero
where an above layer is opaque, where two are), and each quarter only merges its 3D line in: the top pixel is the
above one where there is one, else the 3D pixel where opaque, else the below one; the second pixel follows the
same painter's rule (the pixel on top before the last opaque step). Then the colour effects as before. When the 3D
layer lies under a layer covering the line it is not a step at all and the four quarters are one pass copied.
Exact: a random-stack test of the merge against the full pass (0..8 layers, sprite priority lines, covering
layers, the second line, the raw and the converted 3D line) gives 12000 quarter cases with 0 mismatches
(perf evidence, quarters_test.cpp). render.2d_quarters=off keeps the four full passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
